  <data name="Common_Header_Text_No" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Thank you for letting us know. We understand that reaching out can be difficult, and we are here to support you. A school counselor will review your request and follow up with you as soon as possible. If your situation changes or becomes urgent, please reach out to a trusted adult or use one of the crisis resources below for immediate support:&lt;br&gt;-Text HOME to 741741 for 24/7 crisis counseling.&lt;br&gt;-Call the National Suicide Prevention Lifeline at 988 for free, confidential support.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your safety and well-being are our top priority.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Common_Header_Text_Yes" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>We understand that you are feeling unsafe, and we want to ensure you get the help you need right away. Please know you are not alone. Here are immediate resources available to you:&lt;br&gt;-Call 911 if you are in immediate danger.&lt;br&gt;-Text HOME to 741741 to connect with a trained Crisis Text Line counselor 24/7.&lt;br&gt;-Call the National Suicide Prevention Lifeline at 988 for free and confidential support, available 24/7.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you are at school, please go to the nearest trusted adult (teacher, counselor, or staff member) right away for assistance. You can also submit this form, and a school counselor will follow up with you as soon as possible.</value>
  </data>
